The station has the lowest daily boardings of any CristoCarril station, reflecting its remote location in the highland pass and the limited population of the surrounding area. Most passengers using Coll Alt are hikers, tourists visiting the panoramic overlook, and residents of the few scattered settlements in the vicinity.

